#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:45
#: ca07a7758ee945d78512685de78fd634
msgid "RC Input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:46
#: d64e74fb98f943fca98cc6ebf2c823d6
msgid "The default RC input is configured on the UART1 (R1). Unidirectional serial inputs can be directly tied to R1 . Bi-directional protocols require connection to T1 in addition:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:48
#: 65743ebb796545499a6ad64191ebcf17
msgid "PPM is not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:49
#: 3fb7ddcd004e4264b8f72a972944b3db
msgid "SBUS/DSM/SRXL connects to the R1 pin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:50
#: 4aa4f63b1f7a48159b7d0390e4fd56ac
msgid "FPort requires connection to T1. Set :ref:`SERIAL1_OPTIONS<SERIAL1_OPTIONS>` = 7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:51
#: e730473d7ed1480fa4d95c70aa9b97c0
msgid "CRSF/ELRS also requires both T1 and R1 connections and provides telemetry automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:54
#: b4ef933c475046f4b614e982b421a2f8
msgid "OSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:55
#: 9829f87a75584e8cae44680e5c1e0825
msgid "By default, Skystars H7HDV2 supports OSD using OSD_TYPE 1 (MAX7456 driver) and simultaneously DisplayPort using UART6 on the HD VTX connector."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:58
#: e343587f1892442d88360325fe45eeeb
msgid "PWM Output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:59
#: 159fc0a9ccc24161ab2e44be81133b0a
msgid "The Skystars H7HDV2 supports up to 9 PWM outputs. The pads for motor output M1 to M8 on the two motor connectors, plus M9 for LED strip, by default, or another PWM output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:61
#: 94febf495d884e74b1499e9787454411
msgid "The PWM is in 5 groups:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:63
#: 05f08a7173f64aaa94cc441f7efa1720
msgid "PWM 1, 2 in group1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:64
#: 2b9583c2f9bb4242b5a784aa5316d7f9
msgid "PWM 3, 4 in group2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:65
#: 152792f6d63f488ca9bb98ecc8954281
msgid "PWM 5-8  in group3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:66
#: 4fd47bc11f724fcd8986e5f53cf8e611
msgid "PWM 9    in group4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:68
#: cc0a7e0b44c24f73b42783cf1d52bfa1
msgid "Channels within the same group need to use the same output rate. If any channel in a group uses DShot then all channels in the group need to use DShot. Outputs 1-8 support bi-directional dshot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:73
#: 2aac0a09bf6242c682d544c4d4243d75
msgid "Battery Monitoring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:74
#: 76667199dbbc413b9f1eee083c2404b5
msgid "The board has a builtin voltage and current sensor. The current sensor can read up to 130 Amps. The voltage sensor can handle up to 6S LiPo batteries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:76
#: e239efdff5d74c4cab6f1d6c2df0bb5f
msgid "The correct battery setting parameters are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:78
#: cc9f58621571435483ff25354ad85ac2
msgid ":ref:`BATT_MONITOR<BATT_MONITOR>` = 4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:79
#: 9ecf88bbaff14333836e96de73d90f63
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_PIN<BATT_VOLT_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 10"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:80
#: 64dca7cea9e6447599bd23b78be63f0f
msgid ":ref:`BATT_CURR_PIN<BATT_CURR_PIN__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 11 (CURR pin)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:81
#: dd04f70d29c84d7cb32efa5c9ef58dec
msgid ":ref:`BATT_VOLT_MULT<BATT_VOLT_MULT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 10.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:82
#: d6b5331a46f947f09937e25ff5457137
msgid ":ref:`BATT_AMP_PERVLT<BATT_AMP_PERVLT__AP_BattMonitor_Analog>` = 17.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:85
#: 93376fe909314248a7541fa424cb8354
msgid "Compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:86
#: 26908a3499644bdea8e6fbdbc62f0cd2
msgid "The Skystars H7HDV2 does not have a builtin compass, but you can attach an external compass using I2C on the SDA and SCL pads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:89
#: 41012c11bcd24bbc9b72759ddc955e7a
msgid "VTX power control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:90
#: f7427c7ac1f246efacde9c6bc2ce0397
msgid "If the JP jumper is bridged to PIT then GPIO 81 controls the VTX BEC output to pins marked \"10V\" and is included on the HD VTX connector. Setting this GPIO low removes voltage supply to this pin/pad. RELAY2 is configured by default to control this GPIO and is high by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:93
#: 827991eb0d8b43a98b2d081b17c6fc07
msgid "Camera control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:94
#: d0a1cec10ceb48f2844a0f3c67ccf76e
msgid "GPIO 82 controls the analogue camera outputs. Setting this GPIO high selects Camera 1, low selects Camera 2. RELAY3 is configured by default to control this GPIO and is high by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:97
#: 923418ed4dda4098bd3164fc122d016e
msgid "RSSI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:98
#: 643c0623a269446c9b7b5d4c6836a27b
msgid "For analog RSSI set :ref:`RSSI_TYPE<RSSI_TYPE>` to \"1\" and :ref:`RSSI_ANA_PIN<RSSI_ANA_PIN>` to  \"13\". For RC protocols that report RSSI, set :ref:`RSSI_TYPE<RSSI_TYPE>` to \"3\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:101
#: 7752854cf2544aac8f2511d5e3b9a286
msgid "Additional GPIO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:102
#: 2b0c4ad8947b44cd923c815be64c8e30
msgid "GPIO 83 is marked as \"OSD\". It can be used as a general GPIO pin. By default RELAY4 is configured to control this pin and sets the GPIO high at boot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:105
#: d67af3104c484351bbf17ba905fa2994
msgid "Loading Firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:106
#: c1920d25327a4389862326ad87dd0b91
msgid "Firmware for these boards can be found `here <https://firmware.ardupilot.org>`__ in sub-folders labeled \"SkystarsH7HDV2\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:108
#: 111c82ae86c04d6c8e0f4728a042e6c0
msgid "Initial firmware load can be done with DFU by plugging in USB with the bootloader button pressed. Then you should load the \"with_bl.hex\" firmware, using your favourite DFU loading tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-skystarsh7hdv2.rst:112
#: fcc87c09e1c6451db45ed25f39728fb4
msgid "Once the initial firmware is loaded you can update the firmware using any ArduPilot ground station software. Updates should be done with the \\*.apj firmware files."
msgstr ""
